.opa tabulated cross-section format
========================================

Two whitespace-separated columns:

    column 1: photon energy [eV]
    column 2: photoionization cross section [1e-18 cm^2]

Rows must be ordered by strictly increasing energy. Blank lines and
comments are NOT permitted (the reader uses simple list-directed
input). Out-of-range queries clamp to the nearest endpoint.

Cross-section units match ATES's internal convention (cross_sec.f90
returns 1e-18 cm^2 throughout). To convert from "true" cm^2 multiply
by 1e18 before saving.

Activate by adding to opacity.inp:

    OPACITY_MODEL = T
    OPA_FILE_HI   = inputdata/HI_sample.opa
    OPA_FILE_HEI  = inputdata/HeI_sample.opa
    ...

Per-species files are independent: any species without an OPA_FILE_*
entry falls back to the analytic curve from cross_sec.f90 even when
OPACITY_MODEL = T.

The shipped HI_sample.opa is generated from cross_sec.f90's
analytic formula at 13 sample energies; using it with model 'T'
should reproduce the analytic 'A' result to interpolation accuracy.
